+//
+// The case: the chain's common face U (a rod), walls Fa and Fb standing on
+// it, and between them a concave cylinder K of radius rk below the radius R
+// (a wall's corner rounded with rk), tangent to Fa and Fb along its edges
+// Ka and Kb. No ball of radius R touches K: its centre would run round K's
+// axis at a radius of rk - R < 0, and OCCT's walk failed there.
+//
+// The construction (as the bodies stored in the files have it): K is itself
+// the rolling ball of radius rk between Fa and Fb. With the roundings A
+// (along Fa) and B (along Fb) of radius R run on past the ball that touches
+// U, Fa and Fb at once, each until its contact on its wall reaches K's edge,
+// the ball of radius rk rolls on down from K: between the wall and the
+// rounding whose end on its wall is the higher (the strip), then between the
+// two roundings (the triangle), until their contacts on U meet at P, the
+// contact of the ball touching all three faces, where A and B touch and the
+// ball's section vanishes. A and B are cut along that ball's contacts, K
+// along its section at the higher end, and the ball's two faces close the
+// corner.
